Q. Take a thread dump using stack and jcmd.

 Method 1: Using jstack (Most Common)
 Step 1: Find the Java Process ID (PID)

 Linux:
  jps -l

 Output:

 12345 my-app.jar
 67890 Jps

 Here:

 PID = 12345
 Step 2: Take the Thread Dump
 jstack 12345 > threaddump.txt

 or include lock information:

 jstack -l 12345 > threaddump.txt
 Method 2: Using jcmd (Recommended for Java 8+)

 Find the PID:

 jps -l

 Take the dump:

 jcmd 12345 Thread.print > threaddump.txt

 With lock information:

 jcmd 12345 Thread.print -l > threaddump.txt

 Why use jcmd?

 More reliable than jstack
 Recommended by Oracle
 Can perform many JVM diagnostic operations.

 Identify High CPU Threads

 Find the Java process:

 top -H -p 12345

 Sample output:

 PID      %CPU
 12401     95
 12402      2

 Convert the thread ID (decimal) to hexadecimal:

 printf "%x\n" 12401

 Output:

 3071

 Search the thread dump:

 grep -A 20 "nid=0x3071" threaddump.txt

 This identifies the Java thread consuming high CPU.